<title>PHILIPPINES: Asian Development Bank clears $52 mln loan to Laos.</title>
<headline>Asian Development Bank clears $52 mln loan to Laos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asian Development Bank (ADB) said on Tuesday it had approved a $52 million loan to Laos to finance a hydropower project.</p>
<p>The project, which will cost $112 million, will have a capacity of 60 megawatts and will be able to generate 215 gigawatt-hours of renewable energy yearly upon its completion in 1999, the ADB said.</p>
<p>The loan is interest-free, repayable over 40 years but with a 10-year grace period. It carries a yearly service charge of one percent, the ADB said.</p>
</text>
